{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T14:20:48.939Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented worktree-aware invalidation for `osq serve`:\n\n**`src/core/web/web-trees.ts`** (new, 94 lines) — extracted `singleChangeTree` and `classifyChangePath`, plus:\n- `classifyTreePath(target, trees)` — checks each worktree tree's `changesDir/worktreeFolder` first (returning its numeric id), then falls back to the first tree's active/archive/rejected classification.\n- `treeWatchPaths(projectRoot, openspecRoot, trees)` — the OpenSpec root plus each worktree tree's change folder.\n\n**`src/core/web/web-events.ts`** — hub now uses the resolved `trees` (falling back to `singleChangeTree`), watches `treeWatchPaths`, and classifies via `classifyTreePath`. Re-exports `classifyChangePath` so existing tests/imports are unchanged.\n\n**`src/core/web/web-server.ts`** — resolves `await changeTrees(projectRoot, config)` once and passes `trees` to `createInvalidationHub`.\n\n**`tests/serve-sse-worktrees.test.ts`** (new) — covers worktree classification with the `watch`/`schedule` seams, the no-trees baseline, and a real temp-repo server-wiring scenario with one `osq/001-a` worktree.\n\n**Results:** task verify (`node --import tsx --test tests/serve-sse-worktrees.test.ts`) passes 3/3; full `pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, all tests, lint) passes. Result written to `openspec/changes/089-approve-into-worktree/.run/results/3.md`."}}
